### Cocos Trading API — example requests
#
# The statement's optional "collection for Postman, Insomnia or REST Client" (research R-023).
# Runs as-is in IntelliJ's HTTP Client and in the VS Code REST Client extension.
#
# Prerequisites: docker compose --profile app up --build
# Expected figures and the reasoning behind them:
#   specs/001-portfolio-endpoint/quickstart.md
# Response contract, enforced by the web tests (ADR-0024):
#   docs/api/openapi.yaml
#
# The portfolio, instrument search, order submission, cash transfer and order cancellation
# sections are below.
#
# The submission requests at the end of this file **write to the ledger**, so their figures hold
# from the seeded state. To get back to it: docker compose down -v, then up again (the dataset is
# a repeatable Flyway migration, ADR-0029).

@host = http://localhost:8080
@userId = 1

### Portfolio — the seeded user
# 200. settledCash 753000.00, availableCash 627500.00 (125500.00 reserved by two BUY LIMIT NEW
# orders), totalAccountValue 889756.00. Positions, ticker ascending: BMA -10 / -15028.00 /
# totalReturnPercent null, METR 500 / 114750.00 / -8.20, PAMP 40 / 37034.00 / -0.45.
# No ARS position: pesos are cash, never a holding.
# Side effect to check in the application log: exactly one ERROR naming BMA and -10 — the seeded
# ledger really does hold a short position, and it is reported rather than hidden (ADR-0012).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/portfolio
Accept: application/json

### Portfolio — a user who has never traded
# 200 with positions [], availableCash 0.00, settledCash 0.00, totalAccountValue 0.00.
# Zeros, not nulls: those values are known (ADR-0013). Users 2, 3 and 4 have no orders in the seed.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/portfolio
Accept: application/json

### Portfolio — an id that is not a user
# 404 application/problem+json, title "Not Found", detail "User 999 does not exist".
# Distinguishable from the request above: a wrong id is never served as a real account that has
# never traded (FR-024).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/999/portfolio
Accept: application/json

### Portfolio — a malformed id
# 400 application/problem+json, title "Bad Request", detail
# "Failed to convert 'userId' with value: 'abc'". The id is bound as a long, so this never
# reaches the domain.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/abc/portfolio
Accept: application/json

### Portfolio — two consecutive reads must agree
# Same bytes as the first request, position order included, with no intervening order (SC-006).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/portfolio
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — an exact ticker
# 200. One result: instrumentId 47, PAMP, Pampa Holding S.A., ACCIONES.
# page 0, size 20 (the configured default), totalElements 1, totalPages 1.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=PAMP
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — the same ticker in lower case
# Identical body: matching folds case on both sides, in SQL (FR-004).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=pamp
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a partial ticker
# Identical results, "query": "pam". Containment, not prefix (FR-003).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=pam
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — surrounding whitespace is trimmed
# Identical body to the request above, with "query": "pamp" (FR-007).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=%20%20pamp%20%20
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — nothing matched is not an error
# 200 with "results": [] and "totalElements": 0. The search ran; nothing matched (FR-011, SC-010).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=ZZZZ
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — cash is never a result
# 200 with an empty page. Pesos are the currency assets are paid in, not a tradable asset, and the
# MONEDA type is excluded (FR-023, ADR-0027). "pesos" is empty for the same reason.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=ars
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a whitespace-only query is rejected
# 400 application/problem+json, detail "The search query must not be blank" (FR-008).
# Contrast with ZZZZ above: there the search ran, here it never did.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=%20%20
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a missing query parameter is rejected
# 400 application/problem+json, detail "Required request parameter 'query' is not present".
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a name fragment returns the family
# 200 with four results, ticker ascending: BBAR, BHIP, BMA, BPAT. All four match on their name
# (FR-002). "BANCO" returns the identical list.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=banco
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — an accented name, typed with its accent
# 200 with one result: MOLI, Molinos Río de la Plata.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=r%C3%ADo
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — the same name, typed without it
# 200 with three results, BHIP, OEST and RICH, and no MOLI: accents are not folded (FR-005,
# ADR-0027). MOLI is still reachable by its ticker or by "molinos".
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=rio
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a typo matches nothing
# 200 with an empty page. "bnaco" is a transposition of "banco"; matching is literal and the API
# does not guess (FR-024).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=bnaco
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — results come in ticker order
# 200 with nine results, ticker ascending (FR-013, FR-014):
#   AGRO  GCLA  GGAL  GRIM  LOMA  MOLA  OEST  PGR  SUPV
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=gr
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a broad query is paged and says how much there is
# 200. page 0, size 20, totalElements 59, totalPages 3, 20 results ending at CVH.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — the second page
# 200. 20 results, DGCU2 … MOLA. Nothing repeated from page 0, nothing skipped.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a&page=1
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — the last page
# 200. 19 results, MOLI … YPFD. 20 + 20 + 19 = 59.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a&page=2
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a page past the last one
# 200 with "results": [] and "totalElements": 59 — an empty page, not an error. An overshooting
# client learns the real total rather than a 404 (FR-015b).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a&page=3
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — the whole result set in one page
# 200. size 59, totalPages 1, 59 results. A client that wants everything can ask, up to the
# configured maximum.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a&size=59
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a size above the configured maximum is clamped
# 200 with "size": 100, the maximum in force, echoed so the caller sees what they got (ADR-0032).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a&size=500
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a negative page is read as the first one
# 200 with "page": 0 (ADR-0032).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a&page=-1
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a sort sent by the caller is ignored
# 200, same order as without it: ticker, then id (ADR-0027, ADR-0032).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=gr&sort=name,desc
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — an instrument with no price is still an instrument
# 200. instrumentId 3, PGR, with "close": null and "dailyReturnPercent": null — never 0
# (ADR-0013). Prices are looked up after the match, so a missing one cannot drop the instrument.
# PGR and IRCP are the two searchable instruments with no marketdata row.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=pgr
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a known zero is a different answer from an unknown one
# 200. AGRO carries "close": 138.00 and "dailyReturnPercent": 0.00 — it closed flat on
# 2023-07-14. Contrast with PGR above, whose figures are null because they are unknown.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=agro
Accept: application/json

###############################################################################
# Order submission — POST /api/v1/users/{userId}/orders
#
# Every recorded outcome answers 201, FILLED, NEW and REJECTED alike, because all three appended
# a row to the ledger (ADR-0033). A request that writes nothing answers 400, 404 or 409.
# Expected figures: specs/003-order-placement/quickstart.md
#
# These requests change the account. Run them from the seeded state, in this order.
###############################################################################

### MARKET BUY by size — the exact share count (SC-001)
# 201. status FILLED, size 100, price 925.85 (PAMP's latest close), rejectionReason null.
# Available cash falls from 627500.00 to 534915.00: check with the portfolio request above.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"instrumentId": 47, "type": "MARKET", "side": "BUY", "size": 100}

### MARKET BUY by amount — pesos, not shares (SC-004)
# 201. status FILLED, size 108 — floor(100000.00 / 925.85) — moving 99991.80. The unspent 8.20
# is neither spent nor an error (FR-017). The derived size is reported on the order.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"instrumentId": 47, "type": "MARKET", "side": "BUY", "amount": 100000.00}

### LIMIT BUY by size — validated at the caller's price, never against the market (SC-006)
# 201. status NEW, price 900.00, no fill. It reserves 90000.00 of available cash while settled
# cash stays put, so a second order cannot commit the same pesos twice.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"instrumentId": 47, "type": "LIMIT", "side": "BUY", "size": 100, "price": 900.00}

### LIMIT SELL by amount — the price substitutes on both sides (SC-005)
# 201. status NEW, size 30 — 30000.00 at the caller's own 1000.00 — and not the 32 the same
# amount yields at the 925.85 close. The holding is valued at the price the caller named.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"instrumentId": 47, "type": "LIMIT", "side": "SELL", "amount": 30000.00, "price": 1000.00}

### A recorded rejection — the user cannot pay for it (FR-019, SC-002)
# 201 with status REJECTED and rejectionReason INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS. The order **is** stored, with
# its price and its requested size, and no figure in the portfolio moves.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"instrumentId": 47, "type": "MARKET", "side": "BUY", "size": 1000}

### A refusal — a MARKET order for an instrument that does not quote (SC-009, ADR-0034)
# 400 application/problem+json, detail "Instrument 3 (PGR) has no market price, so a MARKET order
# has no execution price". Nothing is written. This is the one departure from the challenge
# statement, and the README says so.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"instrumentId": 3, "type": "MARKET", "side": "BUY", "size": 1}

### The same instrument as a LIMIT order is accepted (FR-011)
# 201 with status NEW. Naming your own price is the honest request for something the market has
# not priced; a limit order never reads market data.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"instrumentId": 3, "type": "LIMIT", "side": "BUY", "size": 1, "price": 100.00}

### A refusal — a MARKET order carrying a price (FR-005)
# 400, detail "A MARKET order executes at the latest close and takes no price". Refused, never
# silently ignored.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"instrumentId": 47, "type": "MARKET", "side": "BUY", "size": 10, "price": 900.00}

### A refusal — an unknown user (FR-007)
# 404, detail "User 99999 does not exist". The target of the request is a user's order collection.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/99999/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"instrumentId": 47, "type": "MARKET", "side": "BUY", "size": 1}

### An idempotent submission — the first request with a key (SC-011, FR-028)
# 201. Note the orderId: the next request returns this same one.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 7c9e6679-7425-40de-944b-e07fc1f90ae7

{"instrumentId": 47, "type": "MARKET", "side": "BUY", "size": 5}

### The same request again with the same key — the retry, not a second order
# 201 with the **same** orderId, status and submittedAt as above, and one order in the ledger:
# the portfolio shows the cash moved once. Whitespace and key order do not matter — the
# fingerprint is taken over the parsed request (ADR-0037).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 7c9e6679-7425-40de-944b-e07fc1f90ae7

{  "side" : "BUY", "type":"MARKET",   "size": 5.00, "instrumentId" : 47 }

### The same key with a different body — a conflict
# 409 application/problem+json: the key already names a different request for this user (FR-029).
# Nothing is written, and the earlier order is not disclosed.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 7c9e6679-7425-40de-944b-e07fc1f90ae7

{"instrumentId": 47, "type": "MARKET", "side": "BUY", "size": 7}

### The same key sent by another user — a new request (FR-030)
# 201. Keys are scoped per user, so this is processed on its own merits: user 2 has never traded,
# so it is a recorded REJECTED / INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 7c9e6679-7425-40de-944b-e07fc1f90ae7

{"instrumentId": 47, "type": "MARKET", "side": "BUY", "size": 1}

###############################################################################
# Cash transfer — POST /api/v1/users/{userId}/cash-transfers
#
# A deposit (CASH_IN) or a withdrawal (CASH_OUT) of whole pesos, recorded as one MARKET order on
# ARS at price 1 (ADR-0039). Every recorded outcome answers 201, a REJECTED withdrawal included;
# a request that writes nothing answers 400, 404 or 409 (ADR-0038). The body is closed: any field
# besides side and amount is refused.
# Expected figures: specs/004-cash-transfer/quickstart.md
#
# These requests change user 2's account. Run them from the seeded state, in this order.
###############################################################################

### Deposit — a user with no orders (US1 scenario 1)
# 201. side CASH_IN, amount 100000.00, status FILLED, rejectionReason null. User 2's portfolio then
# reports settled and available cash 100000.00.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/cash-transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{"side": "CASH_IN", "amount": 100000}

### Withdrawal — one peso more than is available (US1 scenario 8)
# 201 with status REJECTED and rejectionReason INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS. The withdrawal **is** stored,
# and the cash does not move.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/cash-transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{"side": "CASH_OUT", "amount": 100001}

### Withdrawal — exactly what is available (US1 scenario 2)
# 201, status FILLED. User 2's cash is back to 0.00.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/cash-transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{"side": "CASH_OUT", "amount": 100000}

### A keyed deposit — the first request with a key (US3, FR-015)
# 201, status FILLED. Note the orderId: the next request returns this same one.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/cash-transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: dep-1

{"side": "CASH_IN", "amount": 100000}

### The same deposit again with the same key — the retry, not a second deposit
# 201 with the **same** orderId; user 2's cash is 100000.00, not 200000.00. 100000.00 is the same
# amount as 100000, so it is the same request.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/cash-transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: dep-1

{"side": "CASH_IN", "amount": 100000.00}

### The same key with a different transfer — a conflict (FR-016)
# 409 application/problem+json. Nothing is written. A key already used for an order of this user
# answers the same way: keys are one namespace per user across both endpoints.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/cash-transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: dep-1

{"side": "CASH_OUT", "amount": 100000}

### A refusal — a field that belongs to an order (FR-004)
# 400, detail "A cash transfer carries only 'side' and 'amount', not 'instrumentId'". Nothing is
# written; order submission, by contrast, ignores fields it does not know.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/cash-transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{"side": "CASH_IN", "amount": 100, "instrumentId": 66}

###############################################################################
# Order cancellation — POST /api/v1/users/{userId}/orders/{orderId}/cancel
#
# Moves one NEW order of the user to CANCELLED, with the reason USER_REQUESTED in its history; no
# body. 200 with the order; 404 for a missing or foreign order, with the same detail; 409 for an
# order that is not NEW (ADR-0041). What the order reserved is available again in the next
# portfolio read; settled cash does not move.
# Expected figures: specs/005-order-cancellation/quickstart.md
#
# These requests change user 1's orders 5 and 7. Run them from the seeded state, in this order.
###############################################################################

### Cancel a pending buy (scenario 1, SC-001)
# 200. orderId 5, LOMA, LIMIT, BUY, size 50, price 710.00, status CANCELLED, rejectionReason null.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders/5/cancel

### The reservation is released (scenario 1)
# 200. availableCash 663000.00 (35500.00 more than before), settledCash still 753000.00.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/portfolio
Accept: application/json

### Cancel the same order again — no longer NEW (scenario 3)
# 409, detail "Order 5 is CANCELLED; only a NEW order can be cancelled". Nothing is written.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders/5/cancel

### Cancel an order that was filled (scenario 3)
# 409, detail "Order 2 is FILLED; only a NEW order can be cancelled".
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders/2/cancel

### Cancel someone else's order (scenario 4, FR-004)
# 404, detail "Order 7 does not exist for user 2" — the same answer as an order that does not
# exist. Order 7 stays NEW.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/orders/7/cancel

### Cancel an order that does not exist (scenario 4)
# 404, detail "Order 999 does not exist for user 2".
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/orders/999/cancel

### A keyed cancellation — the first request with a key (scenario 6, FR-012)
# 200, order 7 CANCELLED. availableCash is now 753000.00: nothing is reserved any more.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders/7/cancel
Idempotency-Key: cancel-7

### The same cancellation again with the same key — the retry, not a 409
# 200 with the same order, CANCELLED. Still one CANCELLED history row for order 7.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders/7/cancel
Idempotency-Key: cancel-7

### The same key for a different order — a conflict (FR-013)
# 409, detail naming the key. Keys are one namespace per user across submission, transfer and
# cancellation.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/orders/5/cancel
Idempotency-Key: cancel-7
